5,Gikyode | Accent Network,https://accentnetwork.com/gikyode/,Niger-Congo.Gikyode uses the Latin script with diacritics to denote tones and specific sounds. Text flows from left to right. Phonetics and Phonology. Gikyode’s phonetic system includes tones and nasalized vowels. Non-native speakers often struggle with these tonal variations.,Gikyode,Niger-Congo
6,Niger-Congo Languages,https://www.zompist.com/niger.htm,Numbers in Niger-Congo Languages.à-kpano. ku-du. Achode (Gikyode). ò-kó~.,Gikyode,Niger-Congo
7,"Full text of ""liwiki-Gikyode-20200725.pdf""",https://archive.org/stream/liwiki-Gikyode-20200725.pdf/liwiki-Gikyode-20200725_djvu.txt,'t Gikyode is 'n Niger-Congospraok die gekaldj wuuertj door't Akyode-vouk in't centraal-oeaste van Ghana bie de grens mit Togo in neugen aafgelaenge dorper. De spraok wuuertj gekaldj door zoea 10.400 luuj (2003) en haet de ISO 639-3 code acd.,Gikyode,Niger-Congo
8,Niger-Congo languages - Sorosoro Sorosoro,https://www.sorosoro.org/en/niger-congo-languages/,"The Niger-Congo family counts between 1 300 and 1 500 languages, depending on the classifications, representing alone nearly a quarter of the planet’s languages.",Gikyode,Niger-Congo
